title ALES64 — Lotus's de-esser: the first sidechain composition
prompt baton prin recur — continue the ALES ladder Lindy-first crux-first, sending each finished increment as its own signed round
think ALES63 proved the sidechain primitive and named the three tools it unlocks: the de-esser (a band-pass key), the ducker (a voice key), the keyed gate. Crux-first, the de-esser is the one that proves the sidechain earns its keep — a real, loved tool falling out as a composition of proven parts rather than new machinery.
think A de-esser listens to only the sibilant band (highs where the ess lives) and ducks the whole voice when that band is loud. That is exactly a sidechain whose key is a band-passed COPY of the signal itself: band-pass a copy (ALES46's Bandpass), then key ALES63's compressor on that copy over the original.
think Design: lotus/deess.rye — one function `deess` taking the target, a caller-owned empty scratch key, the band cutoffs, and the compressor knobs. It splices an exact copy of the target into the scratch, runs Bandpass over the span, then compress_key_follow over the target keyed on the copy. The band-pass runs first over the scratch, so an illegal band refuses before any target sample changes; the target is atomic on refusal. Nothing allocates — the copy lives in the caller's scratch.
think The fault set is `tone.ToneError || sidechain.SidechainError` — Zig error-set union merges the shared BadCoeff/BadRange and adds BadThreshold/BadRatio/BadHold/BadKey. BadKey can never fire (the scratch key is a full copy, always covering the span).
obs First build hit a real bug: literal braces in the GREEN print format string ({band-pass a copy; sidechain-compress}) were parsed as Zig format placeholders (too few arguments). Escaped them {{ }}. Then GREEN.
obs Five witness clauses: silence; the de-esser IS the composition {band-pass a copy; sidechain-compress} byte-for-byte (grounding law, run by hand); the key's band-passed level sets the crossing (MEASURE the copy's peak P, threshold P+1 is identity however loud, threshold P-1 ducks — proves the sibilant band not the raw level drives the gain); sign held / magnitude never expands; and each fault refuses by name before the target is touched.
obs Honest scope: from-silence whole-span only, matching how the base dynamics preceded their carried forms. A carried/spanning de-esser (threading band-pass + follower states together) is named as the next rung, not shipped.
obs Fixed a lingering doc gap: the README status line still ended at ALES62 (my earlier status-line edit had failed before the read); added ALES63 and ALES64 to it, and appended the ALES64 body entry.
loom witness=ales_deess_witness green=yes clauses=5 reproofs=2 tame_bans=clean
